## `fetchUrlsWithConcurrency`

```typescript
export type FetchResult = {
  url: string;
  ok: boolean;
  status: number;
  body: string;
};

/**
 * Fetches URLs with at most `concurrencyNumber` requests in flight.
 * When one completes, the next URL starts until all are done.
 * Results match the order of `urls`.
 */
export async function fetchUrlsWithConcurrency(
  urls: string[],
  concurrencyNumber: number
): Promise<FetchResult[]> {
  if (concurrencyNumber < 1) {
    throw new Error("concurrencyNumber must be at least 1");
  }
  if (urls.length === 0) return [];

  const results: FetchResult[] = new Array(urls.length);
  let nextIndex = 0;

  async function worker(): Promise<void> {
    while (true) {
      const index = nextIndex++;
      if (index >= urls.length) break;

      const url = urls[index];
      const response = await fetch(url);
      const body = await response.text();

      results[index] = {
        url,
        ok: response.ok,
        status: response.status,
        body,
      };
    }
  }

  const workerCount = Math.min(concurrencyNumber, urls.length);
  await Promise.all(
    Array.from({ length: workerCount }, () => worker())
  );

  return results;
}
```

### Behavior

| Step | What happens |
|------|----------------|
| 1 | Pre-allocate `results` so index `i` always maps to `urls[i]` |
| 2 | Start `min(concurrencyNumber, urls.length)` workers |
| 3 | Each worker grabs the next index, fetches, stores, repeats |
| 4 | When a fetch finishes, that worker immediately takes the next URL |
| 5 | `Promise.all` waits until every URL is done, then returns |

### Example

```typescript
const urls = [
  "https://httpbin.org/delay/2",
  "https://httpbin.org/delay/1",
  "https://httpbin.org/get",
  "https://httpbin.org/uuid",
];

const results = await fetchUrlsWithConcurrency(urls, 2);
// At most 2 requests at a time; order of results matches `urls`
console.log(results.map((r) => ({ url: r.url, status: r.status })));
```

### Requirements

- **Node 18+** (built-in `fetch`) or a `fetch` polyfill
- Valid URLs in the list

### Optional tweaks

**Return raw `Response` objects:**

```typescript
results[index] = await fetch(url);
// Promise<Response[]>
```

**Per-URL errors without failing the batch:**

```typescript
try {
  const response = await fetch(url);
  results[index] = { url, ok: response.ok, status: response.status, body: await response.text() };
} catch (err) {
  results[index] = { url, ok: false, status: 0, body: "", error: String(err) };
}
```

